  "schema": "fs2-serve.nebius.ai/public-generation-content-anchor/v1",
  "why": {
    "consequence": "The generation name is strong against corruption and weak against construction. It does not make the published trees wrong: a separate recompute on four H100 nodes showed they are exactly what the receipts describe. It means the name alone cannot prove that to a reader who does not already trust the writer.",
    "demonstrated": "The reviewer built two different 64-byte payloads differing in 19 bits with identical CRC-32 100ece8c and different SHA-256, and confirmed both produce the identical v1 generation name.",
    "finding": "fs2-flat-tree-inventory/v1 serializes {bytes, crc32, path} per file, so the SHA-256 that names a generation covers CRC-32 checksums rather than content digests. CRC-32 is affine over GF(2): for a fixed length the kernel of the map is non-trivial above four bytes, so a same-length, same-CRC-32, different-content file is constructed by elimination rather than found by search.",
    "scope": "This is a property of the inventory algorithm, not a defect this candidate introduced, and the algorithm is owned by the localization adapter rather than by this review. Adding a content hash to the inventory itself is left to that owner; this file records the missing identity so it exists in the repository in the meantime."
  }
